# Captain-private local configuration and credentials.
# These are directory- and prefix-wide rules on purpose. An ignore list that
# enumerates private files one at a time fails open for every private file added
# after the list was last edited: config/telegram.env and config/fm-tg-recv.sh
# were declared "LOCAL, gitignored" in AGENTS.md and docs/configuration.md while
# no rule covered them, so a plain `git add -A` in a home with the Telegram
# receiver enabled would have staged a live bot token into this shared template.
# config/* rather than config/ so a genuinely shared config file can still be
# re-included with an explicit negation below; today none is, and adding one has
# to be a deliberate act - which is the safe direction for the mistake to fall.
.env
.env.*
config/*
# Claude Code and firstmate write these local runtime artifacts into a checkout.
# Keep the patterns narrow so tracked .claude/settings.json and .claude/skills remain visible.
.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/first-run
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
.claude/settings.fm-task.json
